snp2.13:10.2 | S: a mendicant would hurt no one in the world; | T: the monk wouldn’t harm anyone in the world,
snp2.13:10.3 | S: understanding the teaching in line with the truth, | T: Having found the Dhamma as it actually is,
snp2.13:10.4 | S: they’d rightly wander the world. | T: he would wander rightly in the world.
snp2.13:11.1 | S: They have no underlying tendencies at all, | T: In whom there are no obsessions,
snp2.13:11.2 | S: and are rid of unskillful roots; | T: his unskillful roots uprooted,
snp2.13:11.3 | S: free of hope, with no need for hope, | T: with no longing, no expectations:
snp2.13:11.4 | S: they’d rightly wander the world. | T: He would wander rightly in the world.
snp2.13:12.1 | S: Defilements ended, conceit given up, | T: His effluents ended, conceit abandoned,
snp2.13:12.2 | S: beyond all manner of desire; | T: beyond reach of every road to passion,
snp2.13:12.3 | S: tamed, quenched, and steadfast, | T: tamed, totally unbound, steadfast in mind:
snp2.13:12.4 | S: they’d rightly wander the world. | T: He would wander rightly in the world.
snp2.13:13.1 | S: Faithful, learned, seer of the sure path, | T: Convinced, learned, having seen certainty,
snp2.13:13.2 | S: an attentive one joins no faction among sects; | T: not following factions among those who are factious, enlightened;
snp2.13:13.3 | S: rid of greed, hate, and aversion, | T: his greed, aversion, & irritation subdued:
snp2.13:13.4 | S: they’d rightly wander the world. | T: He would wander rightly in the world.
snp2.13:14.1 | S: A purified victor with veil cast off, | T: Victorious, pure, his roof opened up,
snp2.13:14.2 | S: among worldly things master, transcendent, stilled; | T: a master of dhammas, gone beyond & unperturbed,
snp2.13:14.3 | S: expert in knowledge of conditions’ cessation, | T: skilled in the knowledge of fabrication-cessation:
snp2.13:14.4 | S: they’d rightly wander the world. | T: He would wander rightly in the world.
snp2.13:15.1 | S: They’re over speculating on the future or past, | T: Gone beyond speculations about futures & pasts,
snp2.13:15.2 | S: and understand what it means to be pure; | T: and—having passed by— purified in his discernment,
snp2.13:15.3 | S: freed from all the sense fields, | T: fully released from all sense-media:
snp2.13:15.4 | S: they’d rightly wander the world. | T: He would wander rightly in the world.
snp2.13:16.1 | S: The state of peace is understood, <j>the truth is comprehended, | T: Knowing the state, meeting the Dhamma,
snp2.13:16.2 | S: they’ve openly seen defilements cast off; | T: seeing the opened-up when his effluents are abandoned
snp2.13:16.3 | S: and with the ending of all attachments, | T: from the ending of all acquisitions:

