snp2.13:16.4 | S: they’d rightly wander the world.” | T: He would wander rightly in the world.”
snp2.13:17.1 | S: “Clearly, Blessed One, it is just as you say. | T: “Yes, Blessed One, that’s just how it is.
snp2.13:17.2 | S: One who lives like this is a tamed mendicant, | T: Any monk dwelling thus, tamed,
snp2.13:17.3 | S: passed beyond all fetters and yokes: | T: gone totally beyond all things conducive for fetters:
snp2.13:17.4 | S: they’d rightly wander the world.” | T: He would wander rightly in the world.”
